Supreme People's Court  Supreme People's Procuratorate

Provisions on the Specific Application of Law in Handling Criminal Cases of Obscene Articles

Fa (Yan) Fa [1990] No. 11

In order to accurately and forcefully crack down on the crimes of producing, selling, disseminating, and smuggling obscene articles, the following provisions are hereby formulated on the specific application of law in currently handling criminal cases involving obscene articles:

1. Where, for the purpose of profit, any person produces, sells, or disseminates obscene articles under any of the following circumstances, criminal liability shall be investigated in accordance with Article 170 of the Criminal Law:

(1) Producing 5 to 10 or more boxes of obscene videotapes, 10 to 20 or more boxes of obscene audiotapes, 10 to 20 or more decks or copies of obscene playing cards, books, or picture albums, or 50 to 100 or more sheets of obscene photos or pictures;

(2) Selling 10 to 20 or more boxes of obscene videotapes, 20 to 40 or more boxes of obscene audiotapes, 20 to 40 or more decks or copies of obscene playing cards, books, or picture albums, or 100 to 200 or more sheets of obscene photos or pictures;

(3) Disseminating obscene articles to 25 to 50 or more person-times, or organizing the screening of obscene films or videos for 3 to 6 or more sessions;

(4) Producing, selling, or disseminating obscene articles, obtaining profits of RMB 500 to RMB 1,000 or more.

2. Where, for the purpose of profit, any person commits any of the following acts of producing or selling obscene articles, such acts not only violate the crime of producing or selling obscene books and pictures but also violate the crime of speculation and profiteering, and shall be punished as the crime of speculation and profiteering under Article 118 of the Criminal Law:

(1) Producing 25 to 50 or more boxes of obscene videotapes, 50 to 100 or more boxes of obscene audiotapes, 50 to 100 or more decks or copies of obscene playing cards, books, or picture albums, or 250 to 500 or more sheets of obscene photos or pictures;

(2) Selling 50 to 100 or more boxes of obscene videotapes, 100 to 200 or more boxes of obscene audiotapes, 100 to 200 or more decks or copies of obscene playing cards, books, or picture albums, or 500 to 1,000 or more sheets of obscene photos or pictures;

(3) The illegal business turnover reaches RMB 15,000 to RMB 30,000 or more, or the illegal profit obtained reaches RMB 5,000 to RMB 10,000 or more.

Where, for the purpose of profit, any person produces or sells obscene articles, and the quantity (amount) reaches 10 times or more of the quantity (amount) specified in the preceding paragraph, or where other especially serious circumstances exist, the provisions of Article 1(1) of the Decision of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress Regarding the Severe Punishment of Criminals Who Seriously Sabotage the Economy may be applied for punishment.

3. Where any person produces or disseminates obscene articles under any of the following circumstances, criminal liability shall be investigated in accordance with Article 160 of the Criminal Law:

(1) Using obscene articles to instigate or induce others to engage in hooligan criminal activities;

(2) Being a principal offender who uses obscene articles to gather crowds for licentious activities, or insulting or molesting women under vile circumstances;

(3) Frequently disseminating obscene articles within society, causing serious harm;

(4) Using obscene articles to commit other hooligan criminal activities.

For cases where criminal liability is pursued under the crime of hooliganism as provided in the preceding paragraph, if the harm is especially serious, the provisions of Article 1(1) of the Decision of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress Regarding the Severe Punishment of Criminals Who Seriously Endanger Public Security may be applied for punishment.

4. Where any person smuggles 5 to 10 or more boxes of obscene videotapes, 10 to 20 or more boxes of obscene audiotapes, 10 to 20 or more decks or copies of obscene playing cards, books, or picture albums, or 50 to 100 or more sheets of obscene photos or pictures, it may be deemed that the purpose is profit-making or dissemination, and criminal liability shall be investigated in accordance with Article 3 of the Supplementary Provisions of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress Concerning the Punishment of the Crimes of Smuggling.

5. Where enterprises, institutions, state organs, or organizations smuggle obscene articles, criminal liability shall be investigated in accordance with Article 5 of the Supplementary Provisions of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress Concerning the Punishment of the Crimes of Smuggling; where, for the purpose of profit, they produce or sell obscene articles, and the illegal business turnover reaches RMB 150,000 to RMB 300,000, or the illegal profit obtained reaches RMB 50,000 to RMB 100,000, the directly responsible persons in charge and other directly liable persons shall be investigated for criminal liability as the crime of speculation and profiteering.

6. The higher people's courts and people's procuratorates of all provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government may, based on local conditions, formulate local enforcement standards for quantity (amount) in accordance with the relevant quantity (amount) standards determined in these Provisions, and shall report them to the Supreme People's Court and the Supreme People's Procuratorate for record.

7. For cases where the quantity (amount) of producing, selling, disseminating, or smuggling obscene articles reaches the standards set forth in Articles 1 and 4 of these Provisions but the circumstances are obviously minor, administrative authorities may handle them administratively according to law; for cases where the quantity (amount) does not reach the prescribed standards but the harm is serious and constitutes a crime, judicial authorities shall handle them according to law.

8. For cases involving obscene articles accepted by judicial authorities, there shall be a list of obscene articles issued by the public security organs and necessary physical photographs, as well as an appraisal certificate issued by the appraisal department. If the people's court or the people's procuratorate deems it necessary to review the appraisal conclusion, it may, upon approval by the president of the people's court or the chief procurator of the people's procuratorate respectively, have the principal handling personnel proceed to the appraisal department for review.

9. The meanings of the following terms used in these Provisions are as follows:

(1) "Obscene articles" refer to pornographic audio, video, book, and picture products;

(2) "Producing" refers to acts such as manufacturing, recording, reproducing, compiling, painting, publishing, printing, filming, developing, and rephotographing;

(3) "Selling" refers to acts such as marketing and distributing;

(4) "Disseminating" refers to acts such as playing, renting, lending, transporting, and carrying.

10. These Provisions shall come into effect as of the date of promulgation. After these Provisions come into effect, criminal cases involving obscene articles that are being handled shall be governed by these Provisions.

July 6, 1990
